{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788632180364,"sessionID":"ses_f8d3af518ffeLlqe3jGkU1uCSu","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_BhdYEALt5mRNzP26df5joLUV","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/review/lineages/luna-max-review-5/iterations/iteration-001.md","offset":1,"limit":320},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/review/lineages/luna-max-review-5/iterations/iteration-001.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Iteration 001: Correctness, Workspace And Entry Points\n2: \n3: ## Focus\n4: Review the relocated workspace boundary, package scripts, TypeScript project references, test roots and packet execution handoff.\n5: \n6: ## Sources Reviewed\n7: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/package.json:6-26`\n8: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/package-lock.json:7-15,1792-1794,5550-5552`\n9: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/package.json:1-34`\n10: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/tsconfig.json:17-21`\n11: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tsconfig.json:1-39`\n12: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/vitest.config.ts:10-57`\n13: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/vitest.config.ts:13-23`\n14: - `.opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/scratch/execute-plan.md:141-158`\n15: \n16: ## Findings\n17: ### P1, Correctness\n18: - **F001**: The root workspace, lockfile and nested package are internally aligned to `runtime/cli` and `@spec-kit/cli`, so no current package-boundary defect is admitted. The remaining correctness risk is unverified because this lineage does not run install or build commands.\n19: \n20: ### P2, Maintainability\n21: - **F002**: `runtime/tsconfig.json:40,51` still carries `scripts/**/*.ts` and `scripts/tests/**` include/exclude entries. They are inert against the current runtime tree but preserve the retired sibling topology in a build contract and can mislead future edits.\n22: \n23: ## Cross-Reference Results\n24: | Protocol | Status | Gate | Evidence | Notes |\n25: |---|---|---|---|---|\n26: | spec_code | partial | hard | `package.json:6-26`; `runtime/cli/package.json:1-34` | Current manifests match the chosen layout; packet prose is checked in later passes. |\n27: | checklist_evidence | partial | hard | `scratch/execute-plan.md:141-158` | Commands are recorded, but command execution is intentionally unavailable here. |\n28: \n29: ## Assessment\n30: - New findings ratio: 1.0\n31: - Dimensions addressed: correctness, maintainability\n32: - Novelty justification: one documentation/build-contract residue was newly observed; package alignment was confirmed rather than promoted to a defect.\n33: \n34: ## Ruled Out\n35: - Missing nested CLI manifest: ruled out by direct read of `runtime/cli/package.json:1-34`.\n36: - Stale lockfile workspace link: ruled out by `package-lock.json:11-15,1792-1794,5550-5552`.\n37: \n38: ## Recommended Next Focus\n39: Review path containment, explicit output handling, hook candidate selection and security-sensitive relocation boundaries.\n40: \n41: Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n\n(End of file - total 41 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Iteration 001: Correctness, Workspace And Entry Points\n\n## Focus\nReview the relocated workspace boundary, package scripts, TypeScript project references, test roots and packet execution handoff.\n\n## Sources Reviewed\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/package.json:6-26`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/package-lock.json:7-15,1792-1794,5550-5552`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/package.json:1-34`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/tsconfig.json:17-21`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tsconfig.json:1-39`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/vitest.config.ts:10-57`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/vitest.config.ts:13-23`\n- `.opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/scratch/execute-plan.md:141-158`\n\n## Findings\n### P1, Correctness\n- **F001**: The root workspace, lockfile and nested package are internally aligned to `runtime/cli` and `@spec-kit/cli`, so no current package-boundary defect is admitted. The remaining correctness risk is unverified because this lineage does not run install or build commands.\n\n### P2, Maintainability","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/review/lineages/luna-max-review-5/iterations/iteration-001.md","text":"# Iteration 001: Correctness, Workspace And Entry Points\n\n## Focus\nReview the relocated workspace boundary, package scripts, TypeScript project references, test roots and packet execution handoff.\n\n## Sources Reviewed\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/package.json:6-26`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/package-lock.json:7-15,1792-1794,5550-5552`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/package.json:1-34`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/tsconfig.json:17-21`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tsconfig.json:1-39`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/vitest.config.ts:10-57`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/vitest.config.ts:13-23`\n- `.opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/scratch/execute-plan.md:141-158`\n\n## Findings\n### P1, Correctness\n- **F001**: The root workspace, lockfile and nested package are internally aligned to `runtime/cli` and `@spec-kit/cli`, so no current package-boundary defect is admitted. The remaining correctness risk is unverified because this lineage does not run install or build commands.\n\n### P2, Maintainability\n- **F002**: `runtime/tsconfig.json:40,51` still carries `scripts/**/*.ts` and `scripts/tests/**` include/exclude entries. They are inert against the current runtime tree but preserve the retired sibling topology in a build contract and can mislead future edits.\n\n## Cross-Reference Results\n| Protocol | Status | Gate | Evidence | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| spec_code | partial | hard | `package.json:6-26`; `runtime/cli/package.json:1-34` | Current manifests match the chosen layout; packet prose is checked in later passes. |\n| checklist_evidence | partial | hard | `scratch/execute-plan.md:141-158` | Commands are recorded, but command execution is intentionally unavailable here. |\n\n## Assessment\n- New findings ratio: 1.0\n- Dimensions addressed: correctness, maintainability\n- Novelty justification: one documentation/build-contract residue was newly observed; package alignment was confirmed rather than promoted to a defect.\n\n## Ruled Out\n- Missing nested CLI manifest: ruled out by direct read of `runtime/cli/package.json:1-34`.\n- Stale lockfile workspace link: ruled out by `package-lock.json:11-15,1792-1794,5550-5552`.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\nReview path containment, explicit output handling, hook candidate selection and security-sensitive relocation boundaries.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":41,"totalLines":41,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/review/lineages/luna-max-review-5/iterations/iteration-001.md","time":{"start":1788632180334,"end":1788632180355}},"id":"prt_072c9266d001wwkPKgvozvcgJB","sessionID":"ses_f8d3af518ffeLlqe3jGkU1uCSu","messageID":"msg_072c8eab2001jUxQLJ0xeLA52c"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788632180364,"sessionID":"ses_f8d3af518ffeLlqe3jGkU1uCSu","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_FQRtUeLCl7CgwRMG5qPmw9OI","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/review/lineages/luna-max-review-5/iterations/iteration-009.md","offset":1,"limit":320},"output":"<path>/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/review/lineages/luna-max-review-5/iterations/iteration-009.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # Iteration 009: Generated Metadata And Acceptance Binding\n2: \n3: ## Focus\n4: Review description and graph metadata against current packet documents, and inspect placeholder and checklist evidence that can invalidate completion claims.\n5: \n6: ## Sources Reviewed\n7: - `description.json:1-30`\n8: - `graph-metadata.json:12-24,42-63,211-230`\n9: - `acceptance-criteria.md:11-28,53-81,85-91`\n10: - `implementation-summary.md:11-29,208-245,247-301,306-358`\n11: - `spec.md:18-32,224-236`\n12: - `tasks.md:65-183`\n13: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/generated-metadata-drift.vitest.ts:1-10,85-100,167-180`\n14: - `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/continuity-freshness.vitest.ts:9-17,46-98`\n15: \n16: ## Findings\n17: ### P1, Traceability\n18: - **F017**: `graph-metadata.json:211-230` still carries an old causal summary naming `scripts/` and `@spec-kit/scripts`, while current source documents and `package.json` identify `runtime/cli` and `@spec-kit/cli`. The metadata also lists `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` as a key file, so the stale summary is a direct generated-state contradiction rather than harmless historical text.\n19: \n20: ### P1, Completeness\n21: - **F018**: `spec.md:224-236` retains scaffold validation placeholders (`REQUIREMENT_PLACEHOLDER` and bare `**Given**` markers) while `acceptance-criteria.md:27` and `implementation-summary.md:28` claim 100% completion. The placeholders are in a scaffold-validation block, but they remain in a completion-claimed packet and require explicit validator treatment or removal.\n22: \n23: ## Cross-Reference Results\n24: | Protocol | Status | Gate | Evidence | Notes |\n25: |---|---|---|---|---|\n26: | spec_code | fail | hard | `graph-metadata.json:211-230`; `package.json:6-26` | Generated causal summary disagrees with current package identity. |\n27: | checklist_evidence | fail | hard | `spec.md:224-236`; `tasks.md:65-71` | Completion claims coexist with unfilled scaffold markers. |\n28: | feature_catalog_code | partial | advisory | `description.json:3-4`; `graph-metadata.json:42-63` | Key-file paths are current, summary text is stale. |\n29: | playbook_capability | partial | advisory | `generated-metadata-drift.vitest.ts:1-10,85-100` | Drift test exists, but no replay is available here. |\n30: \n31: ## Assessment\n32: - New findings ratio: 0.85\n33: - Dimensions addressed: traceability, correctness\n34: - Novelty justification: generated metadata and scaffold-marker review found two packet-level completion blockers not covered by earlier implementation-path passes.\n35: \n36: ## Ruled Out\n37: - Metadata files absent: ruled out by direct reads of both generated artifacts.\n38: - Source fingerprint field absent: ruled out by `graph-metadata.json:223-229`.\n39: \n40: ## Recommended Next Focus\n41: Perform the mandatory tenth pass over the full finding set, final packet state and review artifact integrity without early synthesis.\n42: \n43: Review verdict: CONDITIONAL\n\n(End of file - total 43 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# Iteration 009: Generated Metadata And Acceptance Binding\n\n## Focus\nReview description and graph metadata against current packet documents, and inspect placeholder and checklist evidence that can invalidate completion claims.\n\n## Sources Reviewed\n- `description.json:1-30`\n- `graph-metadata.json:12-24,42-63,211-230`\n- `acceptance-criteria.md:11-28,53-81,85-91`\n- `implementation-summary.md:11-29,208-245,247-301,306-358`\n- `spec.md:18-32,224-236`\n- `tasks.md:65-183`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/generated-metadata-drift.vitest.ts:1-10,85-100,167-180`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/continuity-freshness.vitest.ts:9-17,46-98`\n\n## Findings\n### P1, Traceability\n- **F017**: `graph-metadata.json:211-230` still carries an old causal summary naming `scripts/` and `@spec-kit/scripts`, while current source documents and `package.json` identify `runtime/cli` and `@spec-kit/cli`. The metadata also lists `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` as a key file, so the stale summary is a direct generated-state contradiction rather than harmless historical text.\n\n### P1, Completeness","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/worktrees/public/044-zvec-grep-integration/.opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/review/lineages/luna-max-review-5/iterations/iteration-009.md","text":"# Iteration 009: Generated Metadata And Acceptance Binding\n\n## Focus\nReview description and graph metadata against current packet documents, and inspect placeholder and checklist evidence that can invalidate completion claims.\n\n## Sources Reviewed\n- `description.json:1-30`\n- `graph-metadata.json:12-24,42-63,211-230`\n- `acceptance-criteria.md:11-28,53-81,85-91`\n- `implementation-summary.md:11-29,208-245,247-301,306-358`\n- `spec.md:18-32,224-236`\n- `tasks.md:65-183`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/generated-metadata-drift.vitest.ts:1-10,85-100,167-180`\n- `.opencode/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/tests/continuity-freshness.vitest.ts:9-17,46-98`\n\n## Findings\n### P1, Traceability\n- **F017**: `graph-metadata.json:211-230` still carries an old causal summary naming `scripts/` and `@spec-kit/scripts`, while current source documents and `package.json` identify `runtime/cli` and `@spec-kit/cli`. The metadata also lists `runtime/cli/dist/continuity/generate-context.js` as a key file, so the stale summary is a direct generated-state contradiction rather than harmless historical text.\n\n### P1, Completeness\n- **F018**: `spec.md:224-236` retains scaffold validation placeholders (`REQUIREMENT_PLACEHOLDER` and bare `**Given**` markers) while `acceptance-criteria.md:27` and `implementation-summary.md:28` claim 100% completion. The placeholders are in a scaffold-validation block, but they remain in a completion-claimed packet and require explicit validator treatment or removal.\n\n## Cross-Reference Results\n| Protocol | Status | Gate | Evidence | Notes |\n|---|---|---|---|---|\n| spec_code | fail | hard | `graph-metadata.json:211-230`; `package.json:6-26` | Generated causal summary disagrees with current package identity. |\n| checklist_evidence | fail | hard | `spec.md:224-236`; `tasks.md:65-71` | Completion claims coexist with unfilled scaffold markers. |\n| feature_catalog_code | partial | advisory | `description.json:3-4`; `graph-metadata.json:42-63` | Key-file paths are current, summary text is stale. |\n| playbook_capability | partial | advisory | `generated-metadata-drift.vitest.ts:1-10,85-100` | Drift test exists, but no replay is available here. |\n\n## Assessment\n- New findings ratio: 0.85\n- Dimensions addressed: traceability, correctness\n- Novelty justification: generated metadata and scaffold-marker review found two packet-level completion blockers not covered by earlier implementation-path passes.\n\n## Ruled Out\n- Metadata files absent: ruled out by direct reads of both generated artifacts.\n- Source fingerprint field absent: ruled out by `graph-metadata.json:223-229`.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\nPerform the mandatory tenth pass over the full finding set, final packet state and review artifact integrity without early synthesis.\n\nReview verdict: CONDITIONAL","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":43,"totalLines":43,"truncated":false}},"title":".opencode/specs/system-speckit/054-decommission-debt-fixes/002-scripts-into-runtime-nesting/review/lineages/luna-max-review-5/iterations/iteration-009.md","time":{"start":1788632180336,"end":1788632180361}},"id":"prt_072c92670001VG429e4hHAr0F8","sessionID":"ses_f8d3af518ffeLlqe3jGkU1uCSu","messageID":"msg_072c8eab2001jUxQLJ0xeLA52c"}}
